E=[('Redline 22 · God is the Author; a faith lived, not a book', 276,
 'because it is not mine to write. That book is yours: the one you will write with your life, in the daily, costly, faithful practice of His perfect love. Practiced faithfully, it is the book that saves — you, and your household, and through your household, the world — not by your own strength, but by His love alive in you, overcoming evil with good (cf. Romans 12:21).',
 'because it is not mine to write. Nor is it yours. God is the Author, and the Church says plainly that "the Christian faith is not a \'religion of the book\'"; it is the religion of the Word of God, "not a written and mute word, but incarnate and living" (*CCC* 108). Scripture is God\'s word of love to us, and it is given to be lived: to love the Lord your God with all your heart, soul and mind, and your neighbor as yourself (cf. Matthew 22:37–39). Your part is to live it, with a heart and mind formed by His love, in the daily, costly, faithful practice of that love. And that is how evil is overcome: not by your own strength, but by His love alive in you, overcoming evil with good (cf. Romans 12:21) — first in your own heart, then in your household, and through your household, in the world.')]
